{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head d2bd227fd0386b0f67e5b195c2bcb6f114e8772c on planner/artifacts-sim-20261118, the one artifact `notes/2026-11-18-local-artifacts-simulator.md`, for request b584ea7c under my promise 267ecee7. The implementation is the planner's probe for request 51dd7c02 (promise 723462c8). This head answers my changes-requested verdict b883c9f4.\n\nThe head is two commits on 60223c5c and changes only the note, so no gate is owed. It merges cleanly onto origin main 782fa2b4. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (2 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean.\n\n## The evidence now backs the table\n\nI hashed all 12 files in `artroom-evidence/2026-11-18-artifacts-simulator-probe/out/`, and each SHA-256 equals the note's value. Then I read the outputs:\n\n- `routes.txt` holds each binding call and its JSON answer. It shows `ALREADY_EXISTS`, `INVALID_REPO_NAME`, `NOT_FOUND` and `INVALID_INPUT` with their messages, `delete` true then false, `revokeToken` true then false, and `createToken` returning `id`, `plaintext`, `scope` and `expiresAt`.\n- `git.txt` shows the clone, two pushes with the one create token, the read token's push refused with 403, and git refusing the revoked token on both push and ls-remote (exit 128).\n- `size.txt` shows the 30 MB push accepted and the 34 MB push declined with \"Artifacts does not accept files larger than 32 MiB\".\n- `timing.txt` records the commands, the host load (5.45), the cold and warm start times (1.753 s and 1.775 s) and five cycles from 1.33 s to 1.44 s, as the second-run column says.\n- `vitest-pool022.txt` stops with \"Failed to start the remote proxy session … it's necessary to set a CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN\" and runs no tests. `vitest-plugin183.txt` passes 1 of 1 tests with the local remote.\n\nNo output holds a token. Every token value reads `\u003ctoken\u003e`. Each 40-character string is a hex commit or blob ID.\n\n## One wording point, not blocking\n\nThe `revokeToken` row says that \"the push endpoint then answers 401 to the token\". No captured line shows a status code. `git.txt` shows \"could not read Username … terminal prompts disabled\" and exit 128. That message is git's answer to a 401 challenge, so the claim is very likely true, but the file does not show it. Either write \"git then refuses the token (exit 128)\" or capture the status with `curl -i` at the next run.\n\n## Recommendations\n\nThe four steps follow from the findings, and both of my corrections are in:\n\n- Step 1 accepts an `http://127.0.0.1` remote only for a local binding, keeps `https://\u003cservice\u003e` for deployed configs, and asks for a red that refuses a deployed `http://` remote.\n- Step 2 moves the wrangler pin in its own head and names the smoke check and rate read that its first deployment needs.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The note separates what matches, what blocks, and what it costs. Each blocker maps to one step.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The evidence holds no token value. Step 1 now keeps the host check at `token-reuse.ts:107-109` strict for deployed Workers.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:34dd757308e2351c5f4a5551b166c68f6bcd0934","binding":"assigned","head":"d2bd227fd0386b0f67e5b195c2bcb6f114e8772c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:267ecee7d8c0a5b89cf07ba3eda8717d8667ed0d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:723462c8eb0f097f026ace66d8fbfc446757f87b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:267ecee7d8c0a5b89cf07ba3eda8717d8667ed0d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}